-- title:
--   Fifth-power workspace envelope for finite source construction
-- statement:
--   For natural input size $n$, let $S=\operatorname{scale}(n)$ be the sum of the shared-bank magnitude envelope, local-cover initialization envelope, maximum modulus, prime window, $n$, and $100$. Let $P=\operatorname{maxMod}(n)$ and $R=\operatorname{radix}(n)$. For every starting address $f$ and natural magnitude parameter $U$,
--   $$
--   \operatorname{SourceFiniteCosts.space}(f,n,P,U,R)\le f+200S^5+U.
--   $$
--   The left side includes source controls, retained banks, Pascal scratch, and residue-work logarithms at the scheduled dimensions. This gives an allocation bound with coefficient one on the caller's base and an explicit dependence on the value bound.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/c0ldzy17/three-sum-lean/blob/2b639655e07421b9ac743de9090459bab473a7c0/Submission/ThreeSum/EncodedColorSourceResources.lean#L75-L98

